/*
	The native functions the Permut8 host registers for firmware code, as Impala prototypes.
	`import "permut8natives.impala"` and every call is checked at Impala compile time, with a caret
	on the offending argument:

	    error[E406]: Argument type mismatch for argument 1 when calling write (pointer vs expected int)

	This replaces `docs/nativeCallbackSignatures.gazl`, a `; signature`-only file that existed solely
	so `gazl-validate` could cross-check compiled GAZL after the fact. Impala 2 retired that tool: a
	prototype the compiler reads beats a manifest a separate tool compares against, and this one
	cannot drift out of the language it describes.

	Importing is optional. A firmware may keep declaring the name-only `extern native abort` form,
	which still compiles and still asserts nothing. Declare prototypes where you want the check.
	Do not do both for the same name in one program: the top-level namespace is flat, so a name-only
	`extern native` alongside an imported prototype is a duplicate declaration.

	Entries are in host-registration order so additions are easy to diff. See
	`docs/Permut8 Firmware API.md` for what each one does.
*/

// Kills the firmware and restores normal Permut8 operation.
extern native abort()

// Traces a null-terminated string to the Prawn console, and to stdout (macOS) or DebugView (Windows).
extern native trace(int pointer message)

// Returns processing to the Permut8 audio engine; resumes here when the next sample is due.
extern native yield()

// Writes `frameCount` interleaved 12-bit stereo frames to delay memory at absolute position `offset`.
extern native write(int offset, int frameCount, int pointer values)

// Reads `frameCount` interleaved 12-bit stereo frames from delay memory at absolute position `offset`.
extern native read(int offset, int frameCount, int pointer values)
